          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On January 13, 1979, between 6:15 and 8:30, a witness observed from his home a bright point that intrigued him. This point moved slowly from east to west on an ascending trajectory. The witness took several photographic snaps. The descriptions given and the sky map for that day indicate that this witness made an astronomical observation of Venus, particularly visible during this time of year (magnitude -4.41).",
